{"type":"message-part","messageId":"19a0629c-044e-4953-a8f9-74ed771a34b9","role":"user","index":1,"part":{"type":"text","text":"# Preserving your work\n\nSave a copy of files you create during this task to `/logs/artifacts/`. This directory is preserved after the run so outputs can be inspected. Organize with subdirectories if helpful (e.g., `/logs/artifacts/code/`, `/logs/artifacts/reports/`). The directory already exists and is writable.\n\n---\n\n# Mem0 Metadata Filtering\n\n## Background\nMem0 is a memory layer for AI agents. Memories are partitioned by specific entities like `user_id`, `agent_id`, `app_id`, and `run_id`. When retrieving memories that belong to different entities, you must use proper logical filters (like `OR`) because records are stored per-entity.\n\n## Requirements\nWrite a Python script that uses Mem0 Open Source to:\n1. Initialize a Mem0 `Memory` instance using default configurations (which uses OpenAI and an in-memory vector store). Ensure you have `OPENAI_API_KEY` set in the environment.\n2. Add the following memory for `user_id=\"alice\"`: \"I am currently training for a marathon.\"\n3. Add the following memory for `agent_id=\"coach\"`: \"Always remind the user to stretch before running.\"\n4. Perform a search query for \"running\" that retrieves memories from BOTH `user_id=\"alice\"` AND `agent_id=\"coach\"` using a single `search` call with a compound `OR` filter.\n5. Save the search results (a list of memory dictionaries) to `/home/user/myproject/output.json`.\n\n## Implementation Guide\n1. Navigate to the existing project directory at `/home/user/myproject`.\n2. Write a Python script `run.py` that implements the requirements.\n3. Use `os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")` to ensure the OpenAI API key is available.\n4. Use the `filters` parameter in the `search` method to apply an `OR` condition for `user_id` and `agent_id`.\n5. Run the script to generate `output.json`.\n\n## Constraints\n- Project path: `/home/user/myproject`\n- Log file: `/home/user/myproject/output.json`\n\n## Integrations\n- OpenAI"}}
